            <ArticleTitle>Respiratory infections: a current and future threat.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>651-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1440-1843.2009.01554.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Despite all the medical progress in the last 50 years pulmonary infections continue to exact and extremely high human and economic cost. This review will focus on the human, pathogen and environmental factors that contribute to the continued global burden or respiratory diseases with a particular focus on areas where we might hope to see some progress in the coming decades.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
